.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH crisk-assess 1  "assess 0.2.0" 
.SH NAME
crisk\-assess \- Collect and evaluate one change
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcrisk assess\fR [\fB\-\-github\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-pr\fR] [\fB\-\-gitlab\fR] [\fB\-\-mr\fR] [\fB\-\-gitlab\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-pages\fR] [\fB\-\-base\fR] [\fB\-\-head\fR] [\fB\-\-checkout\fR] [\fB\-\-declarations\fR] [\fB\-\-signal\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Collect and evaluate one change
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-github\fR \fI<OWNER/REPO>\fR
Read the change from this GitHub repository (OWNER/REPO); requires \-\-pr
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress status lines on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-pr\fR \fI<N>\fR
The pull request number
.TP
\fB\-\-gitlab\fR \fI<GROUP/PROJECT>\fR
Read the change from this GitLab project (GROUP/PROJECT); requires \-\-mr
.TP
\fB\-\-mr\fR \fI<N>\fR
The merge request IID
.TP
\fB\-\-gitlab\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR [default: https://gitlab.com/api/v4]
The GitLab API base URL (https only)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-pages\fR \fI<N>\fR [default: 100]
Maximum pages per list endpoint (1..=1000)
.TP
\fB\-\-base\fR \fI<REV>\fR
The target branch commit the map and policy are read from (default: the forge change\*(Aqs base)
.TP
\fB\-\-head\fR \fI<REV>\fR
The change\*(Aqs head (default: the forge change\*(Aqs head, else HEAD)
.TP
\fB\-\-checkout\fR \fI<DIR>\fR [default: .]
The local clone
.TP
\fB\-\-declarations\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Declarations from a YAML file instead of the change\*(Aqs description
.TP
\fB\-\-signal\fR \fI<KIND=PATH>\fR
A signal file: sarif=PATH, privacy\-datamap=PATH, acc=PATH or threat\-model=PATH (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write the facts to FILE instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Output format; inferred from the \-\-output name when omitted, else `table`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
json: The assessment, as RFC 8785 JSON
.IP \(bu 2
table: A summary for people
.IP \(bu 2
markdown: A summary in Markdown, for a job summary or a merge request note
.IP \(bu 2
in\-toto: An unsigned in\-toto Statement v1 whose subject is the head commit
.IP \(bu 2
sarif: SARIF 2.1.0, one result per reason that names paths
.IP \(bu 2
codequality: GitLab Code Quality, one issue per reason and path
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR \fI<TIER>\fR
Exit 1 when the tier is at or above TIER (emergency is above high)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
low
.IP \(bu 2
standard
.IP \(bu 2
high
.IP \(bu 2
emergency
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.2.0
